{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789302689,"nonce":"3B8XeXanUl2TZBlVEsGGuRGJf2Y=","title":"Inline caches are matched to compile-MIR calls by position, which MIR inlining reorders","message":"callsite_ic_data_for_compile snapshots the bytecode IC table in bytecode call order; the backends (Lower::block_call_site_base in llvm_backend.rs, the Cranelift equivalent) index it by the position of Call instructions in the compile MIR. inline_known_calls splits the site's block (split_after appends the tail as a new block) and moves the generic call into a new slow block at the end, so every Call after an inlined site shifts to a different IC entry. The class guard on kind 1/2/3/6 entries keeps this from calling a wrong method only when receivers differ by class: the same receiver class with a different method symbol (two getters on one object, the second following an inlined site) would pass the guard and call the first's function. Masked in practice because CHA (by method symbol) takes precedence for closure methods; reproducible in principle where CHA declines (mir_uses_defining_class bodies, constructors). Fix: carry the IC index on Instruction::Call (or a side table keyed by the call's ValueId) instead of counting positions.","files":null}]}